                        <field name="dc_description">Full title: "Declaration by clergy men, magistrates, doctors, town councillors, Poor Law guardians, & employers of labour, resident in, or belonging to, Dublin, Belfast, Cork, Limerick and Waterford : in favour of the extension of the Sunday Closing Act to the five cities now exempted from its operation". -- Published by the Irish Association for the Prevention of Intemperance, Eustace Buildings, Eustace Street, Dublin. -- [Printed by] Humphrey & Armour, printers, Middle Abbey Street. -- Includes list of members of the Irish Association for the Prevention of Intemperance  containing the names of the chairman, treasurer, hon. secretaries, secretary, and bankers, and lists of names of the vice-presidents, members of the executive committee, and provincial members. -- Includes table of contents. -- Includes introduction signed "The executive committee, Irish Association for the Prevention of Intemperance, Offices, Eustace Buildings, Dublin, December 1881". -- Includes abstract of signatures and comparisons with similar declarations made to Sir M. H. Brach in 1878. -- Includes Declaration on Sunday Closing, followed by signatures. -- Includes handwritten inscription p. [7]. </field>
